// Terms are identifiers, numeric literals, strings, and recursively nested calls.
// Identifier vocabulary is ASCII letters/digits/underscore; keyword case follows native spelling.
// Retired identifier recognition alone is case-insensitive and whole-token.
// All antecedent/consequent identifier terms are operands of the parsed IF/THEN construction.
// A CONTACTS/OPERANDS left-hand label is not a type position.
// Comments and double-quoted strings are lexical mentions; backticks are opaque tokens.
// A backtick token is a specimen mention only in an ERRATUM/SPEC VECTORS section.
// Other prose is not parsed as a declaration. A standalone backtick outside VECTORS is unread.
// RETIRES is a mention section only after an ERRATUM header; named next headings or a blank
// line end this bounded section grammar. Native law declarations in VECTORS are NOT suppressed.
// Unsupported/malformed relevant syntax yields MAYBE, not an invented negative or silent pass.
// A separately witnessed retired law-position use yields NO even if another parse obligation remains.
